2. The Theoretical Conflict (The Paradox)

• Relativistic Determinism: General Relativity states that anything crossing a black hole's event horizon enters a point of singularity from which no matter or light can escape.
• Quantum Unitarity: The core postulate of Quantum Mechanics dictates that the total probability of all possible outcomes must always equal 1 (information cannot be created or destroyed; physical states must be reversible).
• The Hawking Radiation Vulnerability: Hawking's 1974 calculation showed that black holes emit thermal radiation and completely evaporate over time. If the emitted radiation is purely thermal, all quantum state information of the matter that formed the black hole is permanently lost, violating Quantum Unitarity.

